reims-vgpu: the frame mailbox hand-off copies in bands.

frame_mailbox::offer copies the BGRA8 retain (12.6 MB for the vphone's
1206x2622 frame) into the writer's hand-off buffer on the present drain,
under the device lock. One thread did it: a recorded live run on the
development host (i9-13900K) reports offer_us=1473503 over offered=1011,
about 1.5 ms a present, inside drain_ops op0x08_us (~2.1 ms a present in the
same run).

When the hand-off already has the frame's length (the steady state: the
writer rotates same-sized buffers), the copy now runs in up to four
contiguous bands on scoped threads (copy_in_bands, at 1 MiB and above); a
frame of another length still grows the buffer through the single copy. The
bytes are the same in any split.

Offline (banded_copy_timing, the vphone frame into a reused buffer, the host
shared with a running phone): one copy 1.1-1.4 ms, banded 0.3-0.5 ms (medians
of 31). Not measured on a live phone.

--- a/reims-vgpu/crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/frame_mailbox.rs
+++ b/reims-vgpu/crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/frame_mailbox.rs
@@ -387,9 +387,50 @@ struct Shared {
